# formgen build intermediates: IR, layouts, font plans, audit PDFs and reports.
# All regenerable from the pinned source PDFs by tools/formgen/batch.py; the
# maintained artefact is forms/, not this.
/build/

# Stage 2 output (tools/formgen/ARCHITECTURE.md). `forms-corrected/` is
# copy(named stage-1 batch) + the correction ledger, built by
# tools/formgen/correct.py and re-derivable from those two inputs alone. Its
# manifest is written in the same run and binds the resolved source commit.
#
# Committing it would create exactly the 53-bundle PARALLEL CORPUS rule 2
# forbids: 372 files of which 368 are byte-identical copies, that must be
# re-verified on every regeneration and whose reviewed state would start
# competing with forms/ as the answer to "what does this form look like". The
# reviewable artefact is the ledger -- seven small records under
# tools/formgen/corrections/ -- and it is tracked.
/forms-corrected/
/forms-corrected.manifest.json
